---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';
const invite = 'https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt';
---
<Layout title="Discord community" description="Meet other Towns & Kingdoms players, arrange multiplayer and share your next project.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Community / Discord</p><h1>There is room for another workshop.</h1>
  <p class="intro">Find people to build with, compare an expedition’s discoveries and talk through the machinery that finally made your factory work. The official Towns & Kingdoms Discord connects the pack and its players.</p>
  <div class="button-row"><a class="button button-primary" href={invite} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Join the community ↗</a><button type="button" id="copy-invite">Copy invite</button></div><p id="invite-status" class="copy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <section class="section"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Find your way</h2></div><div class="card-grid">
    <a class="card card-link" href={href('servers/')}><h3>Play together</h3><p>Find server-access instructions, check the required installation and arrange a start with other players.</p><span class="card-foot">Official servers →</span></a>
    <a class="card card-link" href={href('support/')}><h3>Work through a problem</h3><p>A clear description, repeatable steps and the relevant log make a conversation much easier to follow.</p><span class="card-foot">Reporting guide →</span></a>
    <a class="card card-link" href={href('features/')}><h3>Share a project</h3><p>Show the finished build and the idea behind it. A few useful details can help another player try their own approach.</p><span class="card-foot">Explore the pack →</span></a>
  </div></section>
  <div class="prose section"><h2>A useful first message</h2><p>Read the community’s welcome and rules when you join, then use the channel list shown in Discord to choose where to post. Keep a question in one conversation so the people helping you can see what you have already tried.</p><ul><li><strong>For gameplay:</strong> name the item or mechanic and explain the goal.</li><li><strong>For a recipe:</strong> include the output’s item ID and the process you are using.</li><li><strong>For a build:</strong> share a clear screenshot and describe the part you are pleased with.</li><li><strong>For an error:</strong> include the installed pack file, what happened and the relevant log.</li></ul><h2>Keep useful discoveries</h2><p>Use <a href="https://github.com/Mikaaah/TownsAndKingdoms/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub issues</a> for a reproducible pack bug or a concrete feature request. Discord is a good place to discuss it first; the issue gives the outcome a place to be tracked.</p></div>
  <script>
    document.getElementById('copy-invite')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const status = document.getElementById('invite-status');
      try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText('https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt'); if (status) status.textContent = 'Invite copied.'; }
      catch { if (status) status.textContent = 'Invite: https://discord.gg/CRYk3uDPVt'; }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
<style>.copy-status{min-height:24px;margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}</style>
